// What reaches the terminal inside `>>|`, and when.
//
// GAP-ZYE-015 (D-09, v0.0.12): what a program draws is kept in a frame and
// shown, in one write between ESC[?2026h and ESC[?2026l, when the program
// waits — here at each `<<|` and at `@~ 0` — and when the block ends.
//
// ZYVM-033: `¶` inside `>>|` is CR LF. Raw mode turns off the terminal's own
// translation, so a bare LF moves down without going back to the first column.
// The tree-walker always wrote CR LF; the VM wrote LF until v0.0.12 and drew
// `>> … ¶` as a staircase. A pipe cannot see this, and the two engines
// disagreed, so this case carries a golden and not just their agreement.
>>| {
    >>!
    >> "ab" ¶
    >> "cd" ¶
    >>~ (4, 1) > "row 4"
    <<| k
    >>~ (5, 1, 1, 196, 0) > "key " 0d|k|
    @~ 0
    >>~ (6, 1) > "last"
    <<| _q
}
